      "construction_caveat_down": "the ratio amplification sqrt(2) assumes the two legs of a pair are independent. They are a thermally gated pair on one host in alternating order, so their noise is positively correlated and the true amplification is below sqrt(2). That pushes the construction estimate further DOWN.",
      "construction_caveat_up": "the median-of-8 attenuation only applies to noise that is independent across the eight prompts. A whole-run common mode -- host state, power, another tenant, ambient temperature -- is shared by all eight legs of one submission and the median does not attenuate it at all. So sigma^2 = sigma_common^2 + (attenuation * sigma_per_prompt)^2, and the reviewer's number is the second term only. Our receipt scatter and the deconvolution bound both contain the first term.",
